course: dictionary
lesson: 1632
title: Chickenpox: a catching illness
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Chickenpox is a noun. It is the name of an illness, mostly caught by children, and it is caused by a virus, which is a kind of germ. «Scratching chickenpox spots can cause infection and scars, so keep nails short.» The sentence tells you the spots are itchy, so people want to scratch them.
explain: Read the words around it for more clues. «Children stay home until all spots have crusted over» shows that chickenpox is very catching, so it spreads easily to others. Crusted over means the spots have formed hard scabs.
explain: Notice the phrases we use: «have chickenpox», «catch chickenpox» and «chickenpox spots». Chickenpox has no plural, so we never write chickenpoxes.
fact: Chickenpox is an illness, mostly of children, caused by a virus.
fact: It gives a fever and very itchy red spots that turn into blisters and then scabs.
fact: It is very catching: it spreads from person to person through the air and by touch.
fact: A child with chickenpox stays away from school until all the spots have crusted over.
fact: Many countries now give a vaccine against chickenpox, and once you have had it, you rarely get it again.
exercise: What is chickenpox? | *A common illness, mostly of children, caused by a virus | A type of cold winter weather | A bird that lays eggs in spring
exercise: «Scratching chickenpox spots can cause infection and scars.» Why should you keep your nails short? | So the spots turn into blisters faster | *So you do not scratch the itchy spots and cause infection | So you can type faster on a keyboard
exercise: Why do children stay home from school with chickenpox? | Because school is closed every summer | Because they need to sleep for a whole week | *Because it is very catching until all the spots have crusted over
test: According to the NHS, when can a child with chickenpox usually go back to school? | *About 5 days after the spots appear, once they have all crusted over | About 5 months after the spots appear | About 5 hours after the spots appear
test: Which sentence uses chickenpox correctly? | *She has chickenpox and must stay home until the spots crust over. | She has a chickenpoxes and must stay home until the spots crust over. | She has chickenpoxs and must stay home until the spots crust over.
exam: Once you have had chickenpox, what is usually true? | You must have a vaccine before you can catch it | *You rarely get it again | You get it again every summer
